		(uuid "709de464-e6b3-4b00-a079-e76cbcc34e78")
	)
	(text "SAFE DEFAULT — CRITICAL:\nR2 (10k) is on GD1 input pin, NOT on Q1 gate.\nWhen MCU is unpowered/reset, GD1 input floats HIGH via R2.\nGD1 drives Q1 gate HIGH => Q1 fully on => motor dead-shorted.\nThis is the intended safe failure mode.\nIf R2 were on Q1 gate, the gate driver would fight it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 72.39 111.318 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7381090a-3d6c-46ae-afcb-eb67c562a120")
	)
	(text "D2 SS310 CATCH DIODE — ESSENTIAL:\nMotor inductance produces a large voltage spike on Q1 turn-off.\nUnclamped: L x dI/dt = 100uH x 20A/1us = 2000V\nQ1 Vds(max) = 40V — would be instantly destroyed.\nD2 clamps the spike at Vf + Vdc ~= 12.5V, absorbing ~20mJ.\nSS310 (100V) chosen over SS34 (40V) for headroom on 16V rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 72.898 146.812 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b936f7af-1ee4-484a-8f70-110f1a97567d")
	)
	(text "R3\n10R\ngate"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150.49 64.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cb3c1b90-9584-4504-83e4-607fd1a226e3")
	)
	(text "INVERTED POLARITY — WHY:\nTIM3_CH1 is configured with inverted output polarity.\nCCR = 0         => output pin HIGH => Q1 ON  => dead short\nCCR = 2720      => PWM ~85% HIGH  => ~8ohm effective\nCCR = 3199(ARR) => output pin LOW  => Q1 OFF\nThis is the opposite of the normal PWM convention but\nguarantees the safe state at CCR=0 and at power-off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 72.39 128.016 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f5c09707-3f08-4fbf-b1c3-6ac06628280b")
	)
